  "observations": [
    "Quest 2 public KGSL source contains distinct A650 and A680 core entries; this does not prove closed userspace supports A680.",
    "A650 GMEM is 1152 KiB; A680 GMEM is 2048 KiB in the inspected source.",
    "A650 uses a650_sqe/a650_gmu; the generic A680 entry uses a630_sqe/a640_gmu. These are source declarations, not permission to replace Surface firmware.",
    "Local Mesa 26.2.4 assigns A650 gen3/3 CCUs and A680 gen2/4 CCUs, with different tile geometry.",
    "Current SQ2 uses MSM DRM, not KGSL; frequency changes do not implement the KGSL userspace ABI.",
    "v819 notgsl contains DRM_IOCTL_MSM_GET_PARAM/GEM_SUBMIT/SUBMITQUEUE_CLOSE and KGSL paths, plus Adreno 680/690 names. Static strings are not proof of reachable or compatible support.",
    "v690 has A680/A690 name strings and KGSL paths; no DRM hints were found by the current static scan."
  ],
  "next_step": "Research validation complete for isolated Vulkan linear RGBA path. Broader formats, games, CTS and full EGL/GLES donor are separate unfinished production-port work; keep Mesa as system default.",
